{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:58:21.951795Z","id":"d5d25c036575c8d79a42b36bcd0ff037ca6859b8afc4a3eef1dcc021b6005f5b","body":{"detail":"With first-take ownership (spec 2026-10-08 M23), the collection's takes make the fixture's live agent the owner of the threads it is delivered, and GET .../threads then carries owner {handle, live, name, person} (spec section 19 item 6 lists owner as an expected additive field). Compared with the committed fixtures/single-owner-21.golden.json after removing every owner key, the regenerated golden is equal. The committed golden was not rewritten: whether to regenerate it now or let plan Task 25's comparison expect the field is open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":877},"end":{"line":890},"content_hash":"e380f23f39bcb646c8d62dafd110ba3cb4e77b3435c48da23a69a1ad4d48704c"},"summary":"Regenerating the single-owner golden adds an owner field to 36 raw thread views; it is otherwise identical","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T16:47:38.362437Z","id":"109c814e8ac8b1e516d72bbf9ab9c4761630d3fc8e96a10da5cf0b40bcad63d0","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Ruled by the coordinator in the Task 15 review: the golden holds when it is identical once every owner key is removed (spec 2026-10-08 section 19 item 6 expects owner); the committed golden stays. Checked again at 1f0f12a: equal without owner, 36 owner values added.","supersedes":"d5d25c036575c8d79a42b36bcd0ff037ca6859b8afc4a3eef1dcc021b6005f5b","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.364409Z","id":"5f44f1de989e3332d4a8270b7d9e8d6e460fe432255b2bed2361b1fc464efce3","body":{"detail":"the_content_tests_pass_when_content_io_needs_an_executor reruns api_artifacts, api_content, api_assets, api_threads and the api_live* modules with CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred, skipping the tests that read or change the home files or call synchronous store methods themselves. A stale skip name skips nothing and a new such test fails the rerun, which is loud; its >100 threshold only catches an empty filter. Content routes outside those modules (for example docs, approvals) are not rerun.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":161},"end":{"line":202},"content_hash":"f198c5e6916be4111196ec404f505223ad4ff56dca8f14c72e527349c488b94d"},"summary":"The Deferred-content rerun skips ten tests by name and adds about 5 s to the server suite; a renamed or new file-layout test needs the list kept by hand","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:37:11.638796Z","id":"6dd9b4184d83df959232bb6b344eaeaa9fc421b9186650e7972ccaf426db8927","body":{"detail":"Mutation runs against crates/clax-server/tests (api_people, api_agent_auth, api_sessions, api_grants): sessionless_narrow keeping only the first narrowing (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs, `Some(a) => a`) and proved_row refreshing a proved row of another harness (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:352) both pass every test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1281},"end":{"line":1333},"content_hash":"3e044e1505a04649ae16a0975ec1470709302b20b947a74e2fed155dd94e7268"},"suggested_fix":"Narrow two sessions to different locations and check a session-less request gets neither's excess; register with a proof of a claude session as codex and check a new row is made.","summary":"No test has two narrowed sessions, or a proof of a session of another harness","tags":["review","test-gap","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:20.904951Z","id":"af8904b3c8011df4d0be08b5ca5635d3f9b1ca350dba70a8e87b8520764d4f22","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:903f2670","summary":"api_people::every_live_narrowing_binds_a_request_naming_no_session narrows two sessions in both orders (catches the first-narrowing-only mutation); a_nested_agent_proving_its_parents_session_gets_its_own proves a session of another harness (a new codex row, not the proved claude one); the PID fallback and the join's wait are pinned by the tests named on 5d0c97a9 and 64fd9bb2. All eleven fix-round mutations are caught (target/t19a/mutations2.txt).","supersedes":"6dd9b4184d83df959232bb6b344eaeaa9fc421b9186650e7972ccaf426db8927","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:31.657850Z","id":"d494907231a2d1935b8081788e7979574f0e7397cb8df554ac5b33d7d50c350b","body":{"detail":"Two mutations survive api_approvals::, api_threads::, shell_boot:: and api_events:: (83 tests). (1) In keep_approvers (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:583-588), Handles::Of(Some(p)) keeps approver for every connected person. (2) In boot.rs:196, the boot payload uses Handles::All for LAN viewers and anonymous callers. whose_approval_a_thread_waits_for_reaches_only_the_people_concerned asks only the owner, the approver, the author, a LAN viewer and no cookie, although its doc comment promises 'nor a connected person the thread does not concern'. Also, a decide_request that does not re-announce its thread (crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1959-1963) is caught only by a_declined_comment_leaves_its_thread_waiting_for_nothing hanging until nextest ends it at 120 s. Bound that event wait.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2456},"end":{"line":2501},"content_hash":"dfadd941db10671133605410494e0f24a27d6f75ae13bb49301e7d238232a7fc"},"summary":"No test covers the approver rule for a connected person a thread does not concern, or for the boot payload","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.888794Z","id":"ae90aa83576fb59f9ba012d5b2a23ebcf555d5ec26cfa9bb6a7a51ed2b5f8efc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86cc3ac0","summary":"whose_approval_a_thread_waits_for_reaches_only_the_people_concerned now asks Mia, a connected person the thread does not concern, and reads the boot payload for every caller; event waits are bounded (within, 10 s). Evidence: three mutations each fail a test: Handles::Of(Some(p)) keeping the full state for every person (whose_approval_..., Mia), boot using Handles::All for everyone (whose_approval_..., Lucy's boot), and decide_request not re-announcing (a_declined_thread_..., held_state wait fails in 10 s).","supersedes":"d494907231a2d1935b8081788e7979574f0e7397cb8df554ac5b33d7d50c350b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:30:59.641540Z","id":"a5c6889e1b5c9c0eaa0a3f6dfec7c2b08956b39d250f68a48f56e4d571e43b0a","body":{"detail":"Mutations run with the api_approvals, api_threads, shell_boot, api_events and api_inbox integration tests (104 tests). M6: concerned() (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:491-505) skips the thread's authors, so held_state reaches only the owner's inbox topic: all pass. M9: states_for gives Handles::All full(false), so the owner's own approval never reads mine ('waiting for your approval'): all pass. The tests hear held_state on the owner's topic only, and assert no mine for the owner only where Sam approves. Add a held_state read on Mia's (an author's) and Sam's (the approver's) inbox topics, and a thread waiting for the owner's approval read by the owner's browser with mine: true.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2471},"end":{"line":2635},"content_hash":"3a530416ffb32bdba7a4327552cfe89e361fc6ec4fe295a2b3d222256324a88d"},"summary":"Two mutations of the held-state rules survive: held_state reaching only the owner, and the owner's browser never reading mine","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.441755Z","id":"f52305d10af72a7703be0ffe62cbfd9bae4f92951fda88284c450c644a2124a0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:628b724a","summary":"Fixed by new tests: api_approvals::the_approver_reads_its_own_decisions (Sam's decline reaches Sam's own stream with mine: true, and Mia's and the owner's) catches M6 (a decision reaches the owner alone); api_approvals::the_owner_reads_every_rows_state_and_mine_for_its_own_approval (the owner reads mine: true on Mia's thread to its agent) catches M7 (the owner never reads mine). Each mutation was restored by rewriting the file's bytes.","supersedes":"a5c6889e1b5c9c0eaa0a3f6dfec7c2b08956b39d250f68a48f56e4d571e43b0a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_gateway.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:30.468062Z","id":"8ece94f2fbd3b2a3cf18cad2caaf0beb6d1f703224d8a2222d0ec4bad7b22773","body":{"detail":"The case asks /api/artifacts/{hid}/approves-first with `tid`, a thread of the live page, so the handler's thread_of answers 404 whatever the gateway does. With the rule in crates/clax-server/src/extension.rs:238 changed to Rule::Any, `cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_gateway` still passes (12 passed); only the unit table the_allowlist_names_each_route_and_the_artifact_it_needs_live fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":294},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"21e1c1ea62544ffdf9a9f1bb153dbf0886508b958631a37f7249d0338de4d19e"},"suggested_fix":"Make a thread on the published (non-live) artifact `hid` and ask approves-first for it: 404 from the gateway, 200 without it.","summary":"The approves-first refusal case would pass without the gateway's live-page check","tags":["review","test","task:23","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_gateway.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:05:29.985434Z","id":"19f536a3c6b2e4142a70e651e632f400bab5d5000df5977f7f9a1596d4a5b416","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:21d2a440","summary":"everything_else_is_refused now asks approves-first on the published page about that page's own thread (htid), so the handler would answer 200; only the gateway's live-page rule refuses it. Mutation: with the rule changed to Rule::Any the test fails; restored, api_gateway passes (12/12).","supersedes":"8ece94f2fbd3b2a3cf18cad2caaf0beb6d1f703224d8a2222d0ec4bad7b22773","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_timeout.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:04:52.464585Z","id":"1be89cf758c09e72d95aa30d0816bc005be1634c76dbf96ac920e4c82c5e29dd","body":{"detail":"Failure seen once: //crates/clax-server:integration__3 at commit 31b71b26, load about 6, assets upload answered 408 'request exceeded 2s' at api_timeout.rs:158 (expected 201). Three reruns (--runs_per_test=3) passed. Each request carries a 500 ms delay header against publish_timeout = 2 s, so any upload slower than 1.5 s under load fails. A wider timeout (or an injected clock for the timeout layer) would keep the test from depending on the machine's speed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"496b99fe92f67149664e5e8c9f732fb62dc0fe0e2a078f7286f57ea0928b665b"},"summary":"The publish-timeout test can fail on a slow machine: three uploads must each finish within a 2 s wall-clock timeout","tags":["flaky","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:21:31.816599Z","id":"7f8dfab537761624b025de18c8f7137c3b05e75e142056029869b83d5d00f0b5","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The test moved to crates/clax-server/tests/common/deferred.rs, which every split test target compiles; the concern is recorded again there, with what the split changes.","supersedes":"5f44f1de989e3332d4a8270b7d9e8d6e460fe432255b2bed2361b1fc464efce3","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/deferred.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.844982Z","id":"4df6b70c7620a5595755894e7aacd6ddb2c73654f6082d34b7411a02cd96a1cf","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/tests/common/deferred.rs:46-97, record 92c3be13.\n\nthe_content_tests_pass_when_content_io_needs_an_executor reruns, of api_artifacts, api_content, api_assets, api_threads and the api_live* modules, those this test binary holds (all under Cargo; under Bazel, those its integration__N target was dealt, crates/clax-server/BUILD.bazel) with CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred, skipping the tests that read or change the home files or call synchronous store methods themselves. A stale skip name skips nothing and a new such test fails the rerun, which is loud. Under Cargo the >100 threshold catches an empty filter; under Bazel each held module must have one passing test in the rerun. holds() names each module by its clax_split cfg, so a module added to MODULES without a holds() arm is never rerun under Bazel. Content routes outside those modules (for example docs, approvals) are not rerun. Moved with the test from crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_content.rs (record 5f44f1de989e3332d4a8270b7d9e8d6e460fe432255b2bed2361b1fc464efce3).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:217836344261c10bd08dc555b813e6df2823eb7c","span":{"start":{"line":46},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"569d77cbd123cd3f8ffa22e89e01e90fb12092dc5cf8113b12b5ec77ee5c7181"},"summary":"The Deferred-content rerun skips eleven tests by name and adds seconds to each server test target that holds a rerun module; a renamed or new file-layout test needs the list kept by hand, and a new module whose content routes should rerun needs adding to MODULES and holds()","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:52:20.537113Z","id":"4d403064ab05092a6986360a1ff5da3310fbfb3d70b49e6c6dd2de15348a3348","body":{"detail":"tests/deferred.rs reruns, on deferred content, the content test modules of the test target it is compiled into, reading that target's clax_split cfg, so it must be a module of crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs, in every target, not a library. The MCP and public Clax helpers it sat beside in tests/common moved to clax-testkit (mcp.rs, remotes.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"55653b2a3989f67b681b525ef79b5ab056f03ac86a3a755b78d5e92572e4b2c1"},"summary":"Put the deferred-content rerun in clax-testkit with the other test helpers","tags":["tests","layout","revisit:Bazel's split targets pass the modules they hold another way","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T15:12:24.892970Z","id":"1c02e0439f8611a55f0e2c5b805935dfe2531b2b6cbff4f1b4452c4de2327147","body":{"detail":"Failure: in one run of scripts/quality_gates.sh, cargo nextest failed api_linked::an_open_copy_holds_one_poll_there_however_often_the_sync_wakes at line 1211, assert_eq!(question_waiters(&rqid), 1): left 0, right 1, after five backstop wakes and sleeper.wait_for(BACKSTOP, 1). The same test passed alone natively (1.0 s) and in both Bazel runs of //crates/clax-server:integration__*. A sync wake that ends the remote poll and starts the next leaves a moment with no waiter.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1199},"end":{"line":1211},"content_hash":"e6dc063f675a42bfb961f462ba0419566aceba390032a7473f8a0d84053fcdf0"},"suggested_fix":"Wait until the count is 1 (or assert that it never exceeds 1 across the wakes) rather than reading it once.","summary":"The one-poll test reads the remote's waiter count at one instant, between polls it can be 0","tags":["tests","flaky","linked","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:13:49.995554Z","id":"57d9b52540a1fbe71903cdd3726993b6d112d883ab7b40d67fd365c331252abb","body":{"detail":"Failure: in 1 of 100 runs of //crates/clax-server:integration__4 (bazel test --runs_per_test=100 --local_test_jobs=12, the six integration targets at once and six CPU-bound processes beside them), line 1097 found linked.answered_there false on a question already answered (answered_via \"shell\", linked.sent true). The other 99 runs passed. The answer and the flag reach the local row apart, and the test reads the row once after the ask returns.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1096},"end":{"line":1097},"content_hash":"c7fad44d4bb1ee98b0eff4e53cdf0b1b3dcf044b6490f60f16ea0fdbcd387511"},"suggested_fix":"Wait until local_question shows answered_there (until(...)), or set the flag in the same write that closes the question.","summary":"a_local_ask_on_a_linked_artifact_is_asked_there_and_answered_from_there can read the local question answered before its answered_there flag is set","tags":["tests","flaky","linked","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_tool_call_ids.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:13:49.995884Z","id":"d549d9cc9ba409985c704ce0ec31c8e3784a8992ecb24f5b25e2c043065ad761","body":{"detail":"Failure: in 1 of 100 runs of //crates/clax-server:integration__4 under the load described on crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs:1096, line 370 got {\"call_id\":null,\"recorded\":true,\"seq\":5} where the publish call's ID was expected. The daemon is no_grace() (CallIdWait with Duration::ZERO), so a report that arrives before the matching call is visible gets none; the test's back-dated event is 120 s before Utc::now(), a wall-clock reference. The other 99 runs passed. Not investigated further.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":348},"end":{"line":371},"content_hash":"6d8a705c757a6f0d3eee28930c98c3310f090bad67bd0376ff6beba330b95915"},"summary":"a_clock_step_back_hides_no_call failed once under heavy load: the hook's report found no call ID","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:14:59.901788Z","id":"e75375fdba5f3bf3066f97cd1ffb253c2553cac7c5a670b7aa74b1b74f8e7ddd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:844c74d2b","summary":"Fixed in 844c74d2b: the test waits for the remote's waiter count to be 1 (TestServer::wait_question_waiters, which answers once the count equals 1) instead of reading it once. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__4 --runs_per_test=100 --local_test_jobs=12 --nocache_test_results, run with the other five integration targets at 100 runs each and six CPU-bound processes beside them: api_linked::an_open_copy_holds_one_poll_there_however_often_the_sync_wakes ... ok in all 100 run logs (grep -l '... ok' over testlogs/crates/clax-server/integration__4/run_*_of_100/test.log: 100; '... FAILED': 0).","supersedes":"1c02e0439f8611a55f0e2c5b805935dfe2531b2b6cbff4f1b4452c4de2327147","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:45:12.360258Z","id":"35f4d20632ac14084abbac761bc318d98439cb22fecb9050ea30c4bb0c847bba","body":{"detail":"Failure: in one run of scripts/quality_gates.sh, cargo nextest failed it at line 1156 (assert_eq!(late(..)[0][\"id\"], qid, \"let go\"): left Null). wait_question_waiters(&qid, 0) returns once the aborted poll is counted gone, which may be before the daemon's handling of that ending makes the answer available to the feedback poll late() reads. Rerun alone it passed natively (just test-native an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll) and in 20 of 20 Bazel runs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1155},"end":{"line":1156},"content_hash":"fcccb7cf0425bb156f3f84259f0ad835713cd911c132254922869bb63a1fa179"},"suggested_fix":"Poll late() until it names qid (with the test kit's until), rather than reading it once after the waiter count drops.","summary":"an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll can find no late answer just after the question poll lets go","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:22:17.261094Z","id":"67ab75345f8b1c35ae708a5ecd19f83925359e14614045dbce4addf37be13e31","body":{"detail":"The module doc forbids regenerating the golden except on a rebased base at the collector's commit. Asking where the person is adds the keys to question views and poll replies, and clax_core::surface::line to every delivery's text, on every install; without_where_to_ask strips that line only when it is the text's last and the golden lacks it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":872},"end":{"line":941},"content_hash":"035b34d6b1e41736a22a2881bd554319c47dc191cd2f7c8f0fa4d4a7753241ea"},"summary":"The single-owner golden comparison accepts where_to_ask, in_terminal, pulled and thread as additive keys and a final where-to-ask line, rather than regenerating the golden","tags":["revisit:the golden is regenerated on a rebased base","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:38:49.694620Z","id":"5b02047a10ebcf73489ca2c21efa0df9ff7082f44873e6325230113bc6699f88","body":{"detail":"compare_with_section_19 accepts, only inside a write whose tool is \"ask\" on both sides, a string that moved from <base>/inbox?q=<ULID> to <base>/a/<id> or <base>/a/<id>?thread=<ULID> on the same base (moved_to_its_place; test the_section_19_comparison_allows_an_ask_url_moved_to_its_place_only). The ask result's url names the narrowest place the question shows (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md section 2), so the fixture's three ask writes now name their artifact. The golden (crates/clax-testkit/fixtures/single-owner-21.golden.json) is regenerated only on a rebased base, never to make the comparison pass (module doc), so the change is an allowance here.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":951},"end":{"line":971},"content_hash":"1424f74298d840823bd8741a6fd1336a31f3308314c54f8b6e650a65bdc1638e"},"summary":"Regenerate the single-owner golden instead of accepting an ask URL moved to its place","tags":["revisit:the golden is regenerated on a rebased base, after which the allowance matches nothing and can go","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.594081Z","id":"ba9aa541c2f63aaf204c2119157f850ab491578051801034ac064079abe49259","body":{"detail":"Failure: in one run of scripts/quality_gates.sh, cargo nextest failed it at line 1156 (assert_eq!(late(..)[0][\"id\"], qid, \"let go\"): left Null). wait_question_waiters(&qid, 0) returns once the aborted poll is counted gone, which may be before the daemon's handling of that ending makes the answer available to the feedback poll late() reads. Rerun alone it passed natively (just test-native an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll) and in 20 of 20 Bazel runs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1160},"end":{"line":1161},"content_hash":"fcccb7cf0425bb156f3f84259f0ad835713cd911c132254922869bb63a1fa179"},"suggested_fix":"Poll late() until it names qid (with the test kit's until), rather than reading it once after the waiter count drops.","summary":"an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll can find no late answer just after the question poll lets go","supersedes":"35f4d20632ac14084abbac761bc318d98439cb22fecb9050ea30c4bb0c847bba","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/golden_single_owner.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.616925Z","id":"a0541f35d45fa69a5826fc1f25019313e67fd854f7830793dbedb58d27fc15bc","body":{"detail":"The module doc forbids regenerating the golden except on a rebased base at the collector's commit. Asking where the person is adds the keys to question views and poll replies, and clax_core::surface::line to every delivery's text, on every install; without_where_to_ask strips that line only when it is the text's last and the golden lacks it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":880},"end":{"line":949},"content_hash":"035b34d6b1e41736a22a2881bd554319c47dc191cd2f7c8f0fa4d4a7753241ea"},"summary":"The single-owner golden comparison accepts where_to_ask, in_terminal, pulled and thread as additive keys and a final where-to-ask line, rather than regenerating the golden","supersedes":"67ab75345f8b1c35ae708a5ecd19f83925359e14614045dbce4addf37be13e31","tags":["revisit:the golden is regenerated on a rebased base","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.640339Z","id":"ddb12a1853a862bc2c55a11616e9f2185619f9ad8a2c4bb4b8e746b2844e4c23","body":{"detail":"tests/deferred.rs reruns, on deferred content, the content test modules of the test target it is compiled into, reading that target's clax_split cfg, so it must be a module of crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs, in every target, not a library. The MCP and public Clax helpers it sat beside in tests/common moved to clax-testkit (mcp.rs, remotes.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":132},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"55653b2a3989f67b681b525ef79b5ab056f03ac86a3a755b78d5e92572e4b2c1"},"summary":"Put the deferred-content rerun in clax-testkit with the other test helpers","supersedes":"4d403064ab05092a6986360a1ff5da3310fbfb3d70b49e6c6dd2de15348a3348","tags":["tests","layout","revisit:Bazel's split targets pass the modules they hold another way","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_app_session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:02:35.345746Z","id":"7d04d3e3410ab1b8cfc067aa53637413e412fa63dda1af7f4ff852eff9fc271b","body":{"detail":"POST .../threads/<tid>/comments answers 200 with {\"guidance\": GUIDANCE_REPLY} and writes nothing when the thread was not sent to the agent (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:523-525, 454). The assertion at line 72 is `is_success()`, which accepts that 200, and nothing later reads the thread's comments, so a regression that drops the app's agent reply (or routes the send elsewhere) still passes. The app worker's restart recovery decides from these comments (an owner comment with no `author_kind: \"agent\"` comment after it), so the reply's shape is part of what the server must keep.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":94},"content_hash":"b0bfae939aa908ffc816d4dc5281d2acb328810f1b78393a36228165ce77e81c"},"suggested_fix":"Assert the reply's status is 201 and that the thread read at line 87 has a last comment with author_kind \"agent\" and via_harness \"app\".","summary":"The app reply test passes when the reply writes nothing","tags":["review","test-quality","flutter-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_app_session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:05:51.886069Z","id":"4fb7a5cfa8a712e7c1e855e33fb54103ad8f6c0bfd5f1208c3a3ba93a7219962","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"app_session_replies_and_resolves_as_the_agent now asserts the reply answers 201, and that the thread's last comment is the reply with author_kind agent and via_harness app, and resolved_by agent:app. With the send_thread call removed the test fails at the 201 assertion (left: 200, the guidance answer); with it, `cargo nextest run -p clax-server -E 'test(/^api_app_session::/)'`: 5 tests run: 5 passed.","supersedes":"7d04d3e3410ab1b8cfc067aa53637413e412fa63dda1af7f4ff852eff9fc271b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_restore.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:13.307902Z","id":"2556b2288c535da1527ecc3d6ab0cca2619a7c261d9c7ccb43f7ef25db87f677","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_restore.rs covers the happy path, stale if_version, unknown version or artifact, missing fields, token, session and the event. Untested: (1) the 400 live_page answer of routes::artifacts::restore (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:716-721); (2) the Conflict that write_version_from raises inside the transaction when another version lands between restore_version's own check and the transaction (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:784-827), testable at the store level by publishing between the two steps or by a store test with a stale `expected`; (3) the audit record a restore writes (kind version.publish, label, note, carried); (4) a publish after a restore carrying the restored version's files and index.html staying at the version root, which pins the new Carry.index branch of write_version_from (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:883).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"017aade347362471b48a3ccba0745286d0aae389394fe26f2ec8843898546b4c"},"summary":"Restore tests leave out the live-page refusal, the in-transaction conflict re-check, the audit record, and a publish that follows a restore","tags":["tests","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_restore.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:24.147829Z","id":"59a8f07ed79ce3d58262957ea35155c5a62d6fcb775bab6d4a5fade3161c339c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Added api_restore::a_live_page_cannot_be_restored, api_restore::a_publish_after_a_restore_builds_on_the_restored_files, store::artifacts::tests::a_version_landing_before_the_restore_transaction_is_a_conflict, a_restore_records_its_source_and_only_unchanged_files_as_carried, a_publish_after_a_restore_carries_the_restored_files (index.html at the version root). cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast -p clax-core -p clax-server: 1214 passed; the 1 failure is store::backfill::tests::the_backfill_changes_nothing_but_version_hashes on the uncommitted db_read_grants migration in the working tree, not this change.","supersedes":"2556b2288c535da1527ecc3d6ab0cca2619a7c261d9c7ccb43f7ef25db87f677","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_timeout.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:08:04.385875Z","id":"dbec06f8329eee8e71fe0e82081dc7f87ed3a0d83d70a36557f1266d59e6f3ca","body":{"detail":"The test sets publish_timeout to 2 s and sends four requests each delayed 500 ms by x-clax-test-delay-ms, so it asserts the real handler (publish, versions, asset upload) finishes within 1.5 s of wall clock. In a full 'cargo nextest run -p clax-core -p clax-server' on 2026-10-13 it failed at line 157 with {\"error\":{\"code\":\"timeout\",\"message\":\"request exceeded 2s\"}} (1229 passed, 1 failed); run alone it passed. AGENTS.md forbids wall-clock budgets in functional tests. The routing to the publish timeout group could be pinned by giving the fast group a short timeout and the publish group a generous one (for example 60 s) with the same delay, so only the 408 versus 201 split is asserted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":97},"end":{"line":158},"content_hash":"87ebfdb7adea28cd73a100a8a77be0839765ff5aa1e0c14c3f2e32b767e2f394"},"summary":"publish_routes_run_under_the_publish_timeout is a wall-clock budget that fails under load","tags":["review","flaky","review:R4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/core_start.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.461069Z","id":"6c7ee5f4f5f148836925f89ae56a7ac078ac53382bbfc94cd13bb456d9c2bec0","body":{"detail":"clax_store::Store takes no exclusive lock on the database (no locking_mode=EXCLUSIVE or file lock on the home's db; crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs), so a second Core::start on the same home succeeds while the first core's store, tasks and journal still run. The test therefore pins nothing about Core::stop, which serve() now relies on for its whole teardown (crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs:449).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"6bdc348b52e07f6e56f8c0fcca1e766e05b14f7280245ce95b658bcad3cf4e28"},"suggested_fix":"Assert what stop does: e.g. the store answers an error after stop (a Store::call after shutdown), the journal's segment is closed, or a background task's handle is finished.","summary":"stopping_a_core_closes_its_store_so_another_opens_the_home passes whether or not Core::stop closes the store","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:18:40.365459Z","id":"7f9cdd482c3b6ff6dc47ece0a5cf5e4eafa1f8905cf58972d9a67f0ac497ec6c","body":{"detail":"an_outside_agents_bad_icon_is_refused checks the MCP text for invalid_icon and the sentence; publish::tests::a_bad_icon_refuses_the_publish checks CoreError::InvalidIcon. Nothing asserts that POST /api/artifacts (or /versions, /api/drafts) answers 400 with `rule` beside the message (crates/clax-http/src/error.rs CoreError::InvalidIcon arm), so dropping that line passes every test. The six model-written icons in apps/clax_app/test/fixtures/icons are checked only by icon_svg_test.dart; they pass the core today (run through icon::problem) but are not among the shared vectors, so a stricter core rule could refuse the icons the app's agent actually writes without a failing Rust test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":344},"end":{"line":373},"content_hash":"91ba09882b8602ed98f5f75325691a8458e7b6c3bc29a3b33666b0819abff2a6"},"suggested_fix":"Assert body.rule == \"element\" in the MCP case (or an HTTP case over POST /api/artifacts/<id>/versions), and copy the six sample icons into crates/clax-core/tests/fixtures/icons as ok-sample-*.svg.","summary":"No test reads the invalid_icon error's `rule` field, which docs/contract.md promises, and the app's sample icons are run by the Dart check only","tags":["review","icon","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/core_start.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.528748Z","id":"f305b67f0aca2e0aba19d4039ba9c9d7e2a9f1d8a6e6c8c695cd0006393381b6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: stopping_a_core_closes_its_store_and_ends_its_streams asserts the stopped core's store refuses Store::call and its shutdown watch is true. It fails ('a stopped core's store refuses calls') with Core::stop's store.shutdown() replaced by a drop, and passes as committed.","supersedes":"6c7ee5f4f5f148836925f89ae56a7ac078ac53382bbfc94cd13bb456d9c2bec0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:35:11.900410Z","id":"4e40dd8b6f49c72cf449e6c74636251f181a8c6952a9e4e3f4b132a8d9c19a5f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"api_artifacts::a_bad_icon_is_invalid_icon_with_its_rule (POST /api/artifacts and /versions) and the MCP test assert error.rule; both failed with the rule line removed from crates/clax-http/src/error.rs and pass with it. The six sample icons are ok-sample-*.svg vectors, held equal to apps/clax_app/test/fixtures/icons by icon_fixtures_test.dart.","supersedes":"7f9cdd482c3b6ff6dc47ece0a5cf5e4eafa1f8905cf58972d9a67f0ac497ec6c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:10:12.310158Z","id":"20c9b7949cfd506d711ebd38a44a377edd379cd9246f01a0516b14dd63496d0d","body":{"detail":"The question poll (crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs, the handler of GET /api/sessions/{id}/questions/{qid}) takes its hold (QuestionWaiters::hold, counted by wait_question_waiters) before its loop's first store read. The test waits for one waiter and closes the question in the store; when the close lands before that first read, the poll reads the declined question, takes it and answers it, so the later late() after ask.abort() finds no answer and 'let go' fails with Null. Measured at 652f225fcffa^ (before any jobs route): bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all --test_arg=api_questions::an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll --runs_per_test=30 failed 5 of 30 runs of integration__6; with an eprintln of ask.is_finished() before the abort, 8 of 9 failing runs had the poll already answered.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1131},"end":{"line":1160},"content_hash":"c0334c082ea901a4bbdd6f258ecdc98304eca99e9239b4be54d66a3d51d7ac85"},"suggested_fix":"Have the test wait until the poll has parked (a debug waiter count taken after the first read), or close the question before the poll starts and assert on the hold some other way.","summary":"an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll races the poll's first read","tags":["review","flaky","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:19:56.893811Z","id":"97eea226145f96dd6d7cc2766098235c40793e1d43221de6c0fb24de7f7898c1","body":{"detail":"Taking the hold before the first read is correct product behaviour: it prevents a feedback poll from taking an answer that lands during that read (crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs:431). The test is what needs a different signal. In debug builds, QuestionWaiters gains a parked count per question: the poll increments it just before its tokio::select! (questions.rs:495), when a read returned None, and decrements it when the select wakes. GET /api/_test/questions/<qid>/waiters gains parked=1 to count those polls (count_until over the same Notify). TestServer::wait_question_parked(qid, n) waits on it. The test calls it instead of wait_question_waiters(&qid, 1) before ts.store.close_question. A close made in the store does not notify the poll, so the poll stays parked, and the 'held by the question poll' and 'let go' assertions run in a fixed order. Check: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__6 --test_arg=api_questions::an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll --runs_per_test=30, 30 of 30.","kind":"comment","references":"20c9b7949cfd506d711ebd38a44a377edd379cd9246f01a0516b14dd63496d0d","summary":"Fix: count a poll as parked only after its first read, in debug builds, and have the test wait for the parked count","tags":["review","flaky","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:00:15.335857Z","id":"5b6ca9c9ea48765a81eff84cf23391891dc7632c8e7c132a84f14b80e82848d8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed as reply 97eea226 proposed: debug builds count a question's parked polls (QuestionWaiters::park, set just before the poll's select), GET /api/_test/questions/<qid>/waiters takes parked=1, and the test waits on TestServer::wait_question_parked before close_question. Check: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1 --test_arg=api_questions::an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll --runs_per_test=30 passed 30 of 30 (5 of 30 failed before the change, the same command).","supersedes":"20c9b7949cfd506d711ebd38a44a377edd379cd9246f01a0516b14dd63496d0d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:43:35.961954Z","id":"a7bb0b681e7fb10b0ad69fd2f4a20337743b7eeb136887799cd92a36adf181ab","body":{"detail":"In a bazelisk test of //crates/clax-server/... beside the clax-core, clax-store and clax-http tests (2026-10-19), integration__1 failed at crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs:1161: assertion left == right failed: let go, left Null, right the question's ID. Rerun alone it passed. After ask.abort() and wait_question_waiters(&qid, 0), the late answer was not yet readable under load.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1132},"end":{"line":1161},"content_hash":"4624f6a0d85afe339cec3b944802eeb088919116387e2b95afe6e149a42ba020"},"summary":"Load flake: an_answer_a_question_poll_holds_reaches_only_that_poll read no late answer after the question poll let go","tags":["flake","session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_briefs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:07:07.075582Z","id":"1aea160b93d78d8d97dcc99542f6dbd19861048f8f7a50cb12c32df507ab31d4","body":{"detail":"api_briefs.rs and api_hosted.rs people_start_artifacts_from_briefs_and_guests_may_not cover the owner's agent, another person's agent by name (withheld), a guest and the owner's agent channel. Untested: (1) a person's agent whose grant cannot read the artifact -> 400 agent_cannot_read and no watch; (2) one that may read but not watch -> 400 unknown_agent and no watch; (3) a live page, which no person's agent reaches (named_agent_reaches live_page); (4) a resolved thread naming a non-watcher (see the docs/contract.md:1459 record); (5) a connected non-owner person attaching another person's agent; (6) on hosted, a member without clax-comments send (ThreadSend) attaching no agent; (7) POST /api/artifacts:new with Clax-Grant or a Bearer cxa_ agent token -> 403 forbidden (DeniedToGrants). These are the checks that keep a send from watching an agent onto an artifact its grant excludes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":274},"end":{"line":361},"content_hash":"27ab7618eb4da39b5606fe7b87593836253d456e615454fe97fac679b007922c"},"suggested_fix":"Add those cases to crates/clax-server/tests/api_briefs.rs (local) and api_hosted.rs (member rights, agent token), each asserting the watch list is unchanged on refusal.","summary":"No test covers the send rule's refusals for a non-watching agent, or POST /api/artifacts:new from a person's agent","tags":["review","review:new-artifact","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_briefs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:10:48.581Z","id":"3f98cbd7442f3de21f8514a1f69ed9b6b0e10118a722e6ec117740d663d7988c","body":{"detail":"`grep -c 'agent_cannot_read\\|thread_resolved\\|Clax-Grant\\|cxa_\\|live_page' crates/clax-server/tests/api_briefs.rs` prints 0; its send tests (:274-361) cover a guest, the owner's agent channel, the owner's agent and another person's agent by name, plus an unknown name. The api_hosted.rs brief test (:5184-5300) covers member, reader, Kim's send and a guest only. Existing agent_cannot_read send tests (crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs:791-810) name an agent that already watches (setup at :94 PUTs Sam's watch), so they take send_target's watcher branch (threads.rs:1210-1220), not the handoff_target branch (:1222-1224).","kind":"comment","references":"1aea160b93d78d8d97dcc99542f6dbd19861048f8f7a50cb12c32df507ab31d4","summary":"confirmed: no test drives the person-send-to-non-watcher refusals or an agent token on artifacts:new","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_briefs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:48:23.333809Z","id":"128d2b977edcf0aa656ac2ab5fc9528b4550486d65f0d78dc4164f1e66d84488","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:47e53f343","summary":"Fixed: added api_briefs::the_dialog_lists_and_a_send_reaches_only_agents_that_may_read_and_watch (cases 1, 2, 4), no_persons_agent_reaches_a_live_page_by_a_send (3), a_connected_person_attaches_another_persons_agent_who_approves_first (5, and 7 with Clax-Grant), and api_hosted::a_member_who_may_not_send_attaches_no_agent_and_agent_tokens_start_nothing (6, and 7 with a Bearer cxa_ token); each refusal asserts the watch list unchanged. All pass under bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1 and __4.","supersedes":"1aea160b93d78d8d97dcc99542f6dbd19861048f8f7a50cb12c32df507ab31d4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:23:32.343965Z","id":"15321fdf8733df1d802d560e39d142bd199c89d848b406697cdd2b58ed7d5404","body":{"detail":"The grouping's visibility rests on q.recipient and q.text_withheld_at reaching both the GROUP BY statement and each group's rows (crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs inbox_groups copies them with ..q.clone()) and on the route taking a group's artifact from its first item's view (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs:371). Today that matches the plain list, but no test pins it: a refactor that dropped text_withheld_at from the grouping would let a person's search count matches in comment text of a page whose comments they may not read (group total/unread), with no failing test. The store test (groups_by_artifact_with_counts_across_pages) and this API test use the owner only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1048},"end":{"line":1171},"content_hash":"6ac3ed68f15e759b841931cac9971e039e4f5462de7e6cce9f42e2c9efbde4eb"},"suggested_fix":"Add a hosted API test: a person with items on two pages, one whose comments they may not read; group=artifact&q=<a word only in that page's comment> returns no group for it, and another person's items never count.","summary":"group=artifact is tested only for the owner: no test of a connected person's groups or of a search's withheld text in them","tags":["review","review:inbox-by-artifact","inbox","hosted","tests","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:26:04.630419Z","id":"fb3dd0beb66ede55c57434e4b3e29ce847c2910794107990d79691e44866c4a7","body":{"detail":"`grep -rln -e group=artifact -e inbox_groups crates web/e2e` lists only crates/clax-server/tests/api_inbox.rs, crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs and crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs (plus .qual files). The one API test, group_by_artifact_counts_every_match_and_pages_each_group (api_inbox.rs:1048), uses owner_thread and the owner's GETs; the store test groups_by_artifact_with_counts_across_pages (inbox.rs:3332) uses owner_thread too. The route sets iq.text_withheld_at before inbox_groups (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs:362-365) and nothing asserts it reaches the grouping.","kind":"comment","references":"15321fdf8733df1d802d560e39d142bd199c89d848b406697cdd2b58ed7d5404","summary":"confirmed: group=artifact is tested only as the owner; no person or withheld-text case","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:21:41.019397Z","id":"22419428979c94c78512e812731b5347d9d5d53eb372dd3da05560434f8204e3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8b7d56ae9","summary":"Fixed: api_hosted::a_persons_inbox_groups_hold_their_own_items_and_no_withheld_text (added in ccee7dde3, its owner comparison by item in 8b7d56ae9) checks that a connected person's group totals match their own items, that no item of the owner's is among them, and that once comment read is taken away a search neither finds nor counts the page. //crates/clax-server:integration__6 passes.","supersedes":"15321fdf8733df1d802d560e39d142bd199c89d848b406697cdd2b58ed7d5404","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:27.030979Z","id":"8cc54cdebbb0306c3bb941ba232588b543239a7600a8f68e3d01df3376af745e","body":{"detail":"tests/deferred.rs reruns, on deferred content, the content test modules of the test target it is compiled into, reading that target's clax_split cfg, so it must be a module of crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs, in every target, not a library. The MCP and public Clax helpers it sat beside in tests/common moved to clax-testkit (mcp.rs, remotes.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":134},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"55653b2a3989f67b681b525ef79b5ab056f03ac86a3a755b78d5e92572e4b2c1"},"summary":"Put the deferred-content rerun in clax-testkit with the other test helpers","supersedes":"ddb12a1853a862bc2c55a11616e9f2185619f9ad8a2c4bb4b8e746b2844e4c23","tags":["tests","layout","revisit:Bazel's split targets pass the modules they hold another way","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:08:23.747204Z","id":"f752b6e470a89a3925eb4a12a450e1375eb8d0dd25e4236748a0a8d7ec428ed0","body":{"detail":"api_inbox checks only the first letter of next_cursor ('u', 'r') and the 'r' literal, and the store test (inbox.rs tests near 3420-3452) checks one unread page and the first rows. Nothing follows a group's cursors across the unread-to-read boundary to the end, nor with an item read or made between pages, which is where duplicates or gaps would come from; the client test 'pages a group's new items first, then its read ones' does so against a mock (inbox-page.test.ts groupsOf), not the daemon.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1165},"end":{"line":1198},"content_hash":"c145a34516b6505ec2f5c4df25df51fdd77fd87cdfda89bf983e51a0739b7be0"},"suggested_fix":"Add an api_inbox test that follows a group's next_cursor (u<seq> with read=unread, then r / r<seq> with read=read) until null and asserts the IDs equal the group's matches once each, with one item read between pages.","summary":"No test pages a group to the end through u<seq>, r and r<seq> and checks every item appears exactly once","tags":["review","review:inbox-one-list","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:10:19.182673Z","id":"66572f98ae8da53e959e036bab090b03faa6f7ea37482cc7642668e943d951b1","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_inbox.rs:1104-1110 follows one u<seq> step with read=unread (5 items) and stops; :1165-1168, :1189-1192 and :1198 only check the cursor starts with 'r' or equals \"r\"; no test requests read=read with r/r<seq> until next_cursor is null. crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:3381-3445 (groups_by_artifact_with_counts_across_pages) checks one unread page via inbox_list and the first rows' shape, not a walk through the read part. web/e2e/inbox.spec.ts:74-76 clicks Show more against the daemon, but the Sales group there is all unread, so the read part is never paged. A suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"f752b6e470a89a3925eb4a12a450e1375eb8d0dd25e4236748a0a8d7ec428ed0","summary":"confirmed: no daemon test follows a group's cursors across the unread-to-read boundary to the end","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:21:40.496211Z","id":"a85c40590d1d1260bfe0f09b108aea0b4f0cd1b9c44ed97669e83a6b12784b1a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:60d96fe07","summary":"Fixed: api_inbox::a_group_pages_through_its_cursors_to_the_end_listing_each_item_once follows a group's u<seq>, r and r<seq> cursors to the end with an unlisted item read between pages, and checks every item of the group is listed exactly once. It passes in //crates/clax-server:integration__3.","supersedes":"f752b6e470a89a3925eb4a12a450e1375eb8d0dd25e4236748a0a8d7ec428ed0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:53:17.993081Z","id":"1665958d4be16fd4f4d09c981ac68d55b562016b79840801d0899d0355ed0138","body":{"detail":"people_guests_and_agents_apply_tags_only_where_they_administer covers the owner's token agent, a collaborator's agent, an editor (clax:full), a reader, a connected person's browser, a guest and no credential, but no Caller::PersonAgent { person: None } (which manages the list and administers every artifact: crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs:38-43, crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:956) and no person's agent whose grant lacks clax-artifacts update at its own person's artifact (which the need ArtifactTagsPut must refuse 403 not_permitted although administers says yes). Both are the paths where the route's own check and the need's disagree, and b15019d5 leaves the first open for a decision.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":233},"end":{"line":434},"content_hash":"4dfaab85891bd3a5ace5c1a6a5cc955e505e3b0e07aeb75974171bf8d8a5f33b"},"suggested_fix":"Add both callers to the test, asserting whatever b15019d5 decides for the first and 403 not_permitted for the second.","summary":"The tag routes' caller matrix has no case for a grant of the owner's row or for a narrowed own-artifact grant","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags","tests","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:55:11.180630Z","id":"b4e66c260ff3e3ba236947f0825f9eb08a4ca22ac1c621b633fc0a9f05b7eea7","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_tags.rs:233-434 exercises Sam's agent, Ed (clax:full), Mia's browser, the owner's agent, Gil (guest), no credential and Rae (clax:reader); none is Caller::PersonAgent { person: None }, which manages_tags (crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs:38-43) and administers (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:956) both admit. The only 'locations: [own]' grant in the file is at :627 in counts_follow_what_the_caller_sees_and_guests_see_only_tags_in_use, a read-only grant used for GET /api/tags counts, not a tag write.","kind":"comment","references":"1665958d4be16fd4f4d09c981ac68d55b562016b79840801d0899d0355ed0138","summary":"confirmed: the caller matrix has no owner-row grant agent and no narrowed own-artifact grant","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:14:34.805970Z","id":"dc3ba6f22cc309daaf93523faa39c19e8ba0c9c44278759a1cb64f503ed1057f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bffaeb4d0","summary":"Fixed in bffaeb4d0: api_tags::a_grant_of_the_owners_row_manages_tags_and_applies_them_anywhere and api_tags::a_persons_agent_without_update_tags_not_even_its_own_persons_artifact (403 not_permitted, right update) pass (bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all PASSED)","supersedes":"1665958d4be16fd4f4d09c981ac68d55b562016b79840801d0899d0355ed0138","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:00.429913Z","id":"76872e37d5daf815eb3915428beccca97b4106579b134452428c6a7ff11d0389","body":{"detail":"tests/deferred.rs reruns, on deferred content, the content test modules of the test target it is compiled into, reading that target's clax_split cfg, so it must be a module of crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs, in every target, not a library. The MCP and public Clax helpers it sat beside in tests/common moved to clax-testkit (mcp.rs, remotes.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"55653b2a3989f67b681b525ef79b5ab056f03ac86a3a755b78d5e92572e4b2c1"},"summary":"Put the deferred-content rerun in clax-testkit with the other test helpers","supersedes":"8cc54cdebbb0306c3bb941ba232588b543239a7600a8f68e3d01df3376af745e","tags":["tests","layout","revisit:Bazel's split targets pass the modules they hold another way","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:48:33.479772Z","id":"728c977058c6ff42c35abdf1e42d469524a1aa116854c3f49ddacb1f0109cd74","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:84eaa4553","summary":"Root cause: the hold starts before the poll's first read, so a poll slower than the test's close read the question declined and took the answer itself. The test now closes it only after wait_parked_question_polls. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1..6 --runs_per_test=10 with this test as filter, load average 60-230: 10 of 10 passed, twice.","supersedes":"a7bb0b681e7fb10b0ad69fd2f4a20337743b7eeb136887799cd92a36adf181ab","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:48:33.604912Z","id":"12d178b13f12f957dce6a46ef858f734863b8c0f34ba3b4d751fcb52a829fafd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:84eaa4553","summary":"Same flake as a7bb0b68, fixed by closing the question only after the poll parks (wait_parked_question_polls). Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1..6 --runs_per_test=10 with this test as filter, load average 60-230: 10 of 10 passed, twice.","supersedes":"ba9aa541c2f63aaf204c2119157f850ab491578051801034ac064079abe49259","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T16:40:19.199778Z","id":"b224f2931e2d9d9eb8c7b44350e0a00f9bc81b0f33c3f6f90c225ebbad2f20fc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3d848b1af","summary":"Fixed in 3d848b1af: the test waits with until() for linked.answered_there instead of reading the row once after the ask's wait ends. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1..__6 --runs_per_test=10 --nocache_test_results on macOS (60 runs, 12 at once): 'a_local_ask_on_a_linked_artifact_is_asked_there_and_answered_from_there ... ok' in all 10 run logs of integration__5, FAILED in none.","supersedes":"57d9b52540a1fbe71903cdd3726993b6d112d883ab7b40d67fd365c331252abb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_timeout.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T16:40:20.756481Z","id":"1ff019602d6d9270ad3a9f4646db1de9a99bd61f84d999d59fe07838ce7864a1","body":{"detail":"Failure: under bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1..__6 --runs_per_test=10 on macOS (12 test processes at once), integration__5 failed it in 3 of 10 runs: at line 70 the publish answered 201 instead of 408, and once line 76 found no artifacts array. The outcome depends on which of two wall-clock durations ends first on a loaded machine. Not seen in CI.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"91804d5404cbd794f8c58a3772d6c804b95c2995ed5aa21c97ebc1139c577839"},"summary":"write_side_effects_survive_a_handler_timeout races a 100 ms request timeout against a 300 ms handler","tags":["tests","flaky","wall-clock","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_sample.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T16:40:20.756712Z","id":"2bc137892019f270e375185e1b4c29347b7dbce5637051137a1e443ac2236645","body":{"detail":"Failure: under bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1..__6 --runs_per_test=10 on macOS (12 test processes at once), integration__5 failed it once at line 827 (expect(\"refused\")): the flooder's next call was accepted because the held calls had not all reached the daemon within the 300 ms sleep. Not seen in CI.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":817},"end":{"line":827},"content_hash":"fe8b6bdfd8c9c37664fc39426c570ad6b1f2693dfb710a862a8cb04869d90ebf"},"summary":"a_flood_from_one_viewer_is_rate_limited sleeps 300 ms in place of waiting for the held calls","tags":["tests","flaky","wall-clock","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_timeout.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:27:46.470552Z","id":"55a84103d109a7ddd42b481b7366b4b7a1d2bd9d3d244477305875ca80cb5cd7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:baf7b4a4f","summary":"Fixed: the store call of /api/_test/slow_publish/{ms}?after_drop=true makes the artifact only once the timed-out handler is dropped, and the count is read from the store, not a GET under the 100 ms timeout. bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__5 --runs_per_test=50, twice, beside 12 busy-loop processes (load average 78-114): 100 of 100 runs passed.","supersedes":"1ff019602d6d9270ad3a9f4646db1de9a99bd61f84d999d59fe07838ce7864a1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_timeout.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:27:47.048883Z","id":"e308b8a8a850414f1d942b957bc4daacf4568a08dcd388d1d28f58e0798f9d9f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f9cabf43b","summary":"Fixed: the test sets distinct limits (100 ms, 200 ms), holds each request 60 s, and checks that each 408 names its route group's limit, so no request must finish within a wall-clock budget. Under 12 busy-loop processes, bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__5 --runs_per_test=50 failed it in 5 of 50 runs before (api_timeout.rs:125 and :142, 201 expected) and passed 100 of 100 runs (2 x 50) after.","supersedes":"1be89cf758c09e72d95aa30d0816bc005be1634c76dbf96ac920e4c82c5e29dd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_sample.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:27:47.586053Z","id":"9ac6ed10bea120854a53a9afe599b79401698339b11d2aa822552f1fa073445d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:39d5786dc","summary":"Fixed: the held calls wait on a tool that never answers, and the test polls the flooder's ViewerQueues until enter() refuses a place before making the call that must be refused; no sleep stands in for the condition. bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__5 --runs_per_test=50, twice, beside 12 busy-loop processes (load average 78-114): 100 of 100 runs passed.","supersedes":"2bc137892019f270e375185e1b4c29347b7dbce5637051137a1e443ac2236645","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:19.109109Z","id":"43d09d39a37f6d29602059a7e3132fe431f473a5010b08151f6636d0954f9ab6","body":{"detail":"The test opens 150 connections to the daemon at once. Where the listen backlog is smaller (macOS caps it at kern.ipc.somaxconn, 128 by default), connects beyond it are reset and the test panics at crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs:80 with reqwest ConnectError 'Connection reset by peer' (os error 54). It fails the same way at 4ad6c68b, before the site host lookup, and alone: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__6 --test_arg=api_seats --nocache_test_results (7 passed, 1 failed, on a machine with kern.ipc.somaxconn: 128).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":407},"end":{"line":509},"content_hash":"21e1bad5ec9889fe3e7bc49ade114cab2f77b50f7b770842ea9bb99e260e2bfd"},"summary":"load_150_people_on_100_seats fails with connection resets where the listen backlog is below 150","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:39:37.374057Z","id":"77b7b3ccf1aa7500db6928bdc1b9797fc2842e2685a7e5bc0493d998b0f17396","body":{"detail":"At 86ec4f43 bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__6 --test_arg=load_150 failed 3 of 3 runs alone and once in just ci: reqwest ConnectionReset (os error 54) at TCP connect to POST /api/stream/<id>, with 150 event streams already open and 150 POSTs sent at once; kern.ipc.somaxconn is 128 here. The test exercises only loopback /api/stream routes, which this change did not touch; an earlier run in the same session passed alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":409},"end":{"line":409},"content_hash":"ce4f9ea1ef7c2267c1113e0df6f7088f93fb1d15c64f86a3af6d9691cd8b2310"},"summary":"load_150_people_on_100_seats fails with a connection reset on this machine, alone and in the suite","tags":["flake","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:56.645522Z","id":"7a6aa55ffe54d8b6f2dbab9c7186bd9d6a1e7d375d798bc7431b1cfb70a60397","body":{"detail":"Seen in bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__2 at api_seats.rs:80, the stream helper it calls (reqwest ConnectError, Os code 54), on the full shard and again alone; the machine's load average was about 20. The test opens 150 streams at once; the listen backlog or the per-process descriptor limit may be what resets them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":408},"end":{"line":509},"content_hash":"6485dd280f03ce2eafc89515875749bd47c212582bc6a69ad25794a8eebff13b"},"summary":"api_seats::load_150_people_on_100_seats failed twice in a row with 'Connection reset by peer' opening /api/stream on a loaded macOS machine","tags":["flaky","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.233677Z","id":"24a0ae11faff5765487bdae19900ddac66218a06e8e5f5355fd3831952c271a7","body":{"detail":"tests/deferred.rs reruns, on deferred content, the content test modules of the test target it is compiled into, reading that target's clax_split cfg, so it must be a module of crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs, in every target, not a library. The MCP and public Clax helpers it sat beside in tests/common moved to clax-testkit (mcp.rs, remotes.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":142},"end":{"line":142},"content_hash":"55653b2a3989f67b681b525ef79b5ab056f03ac86a3a755b78d5e92572e4b2c1"},"summary":"Put the deferred-content rerun in clax-testkit with the other test helpers","supersedes":"76872e37d5daf815eb3915428beccca97b4106579b134452428c6a7ff11d0389","tags":["tests","layout","revisit:Bazel's split targets pass the modules they hold another way","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.408819Z","id":"6ff421d8b6721035a644e3b409d2ff8aee1ff8b7b9c60da7ec3be37d03ac7a54","body":{"detail":"tests/deferred.rs reruns, on deferred content, the content test modules of the test target it is compiled into, reading that target's clax_split cfg, so it must be a module of crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs, in every target, not a library. The MCP and public Clax helpers it sat beside in tests/common moved to clax-testkit (mcp.rs, remotes.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"55653b2a3989f67b681b525ef79b5ab056f03ac86a3a755b78d5e92572e4b2c1"},"summary":"Put the deferred-content rerun in clax-testkit with the other test helpers","supersedes":"24a0ae11faff5765487bdae19900ddac66218a06e8e5f5355fd3831952c271a7","tags":["tests","layout","revisit:Bazel's split targets pass the modules they hold another way","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:19:51.257102Z","id":"959b097846601d4db6e76336dda7ee310fcbeeda130e9b49884ce8a13e4a2b8e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7a6aa55ffe54d8b6f2dbab9c7186bd9d6a1e7d375d798bc7431b1cfb70a60397","summary":"Seen again on macOS 27.0.1 (kern.ipc.somaxconn 128): failed in a full just check and again run alone (bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__6), each time a 'Connection reset by peer' on a POST /api/stream/<id> at crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs:80. 150 connections in a burst exceed a 128 listen backlog; unconfirmed as the cause.","tags":["session:claude-code:a63eca05-dc63-499b-9f6d-066bae1fb314"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_quickstart.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T02:27:30.517224Z","id":"d46abbbac0aada9b1767bc23fb339cf8cb02cd915394ef518be13e3cd6671c0a","body":{"detail":"The test asserts only that the response body lacks the page's text; a 200 with other content, or any status, passes. Assert the status the shell origin answers (404) as well.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":5},"end":{"line":19},"content_hash":"e71cf30240b32189b10f86940a7821363e0871fb14366cefe9bbfe1f4200d886"},"summary":"the_shell_origin_serves_no_quickstart_file checks the body, not the status","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T14:50:49.813275Z","id":"d09226f4c49124c5d3430e7cca2bde727167d5fe086d7bccbd78d30efcb02cbf","body":{"detail":"bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__2 failed twice before 74d6b37ad (Connection reset by peer at api_seats.rs:80) and passed with --runs_per_test=3 at it; scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci passed whole at 8c4269509 (357 of 357 tests): 'Stats over 3 runs', 'Executed 1 out of 1 test: 1 test passes'.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:74d6b37ad","summary":"Fixed: the test's 150 concurrent seat requests now go at most 64 at a time (IN_FLIGHT), below macOS's kern.ipc.somaxconn of 128","supersedes":"43d09d39a37f6d29602059a7e3132fe431f473a5010b08151f6636d0954f9ab6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T14:50:49.895226Z","id":"66ff42aa475d92050252077cb40f067c43d7f8566a2c37cb1043389728221f70","body":{"detail":"bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__2 failed twice before 74d6b37ad (Connection reset by peer at api_seats.rs:80) and passed with --runs_per_test=3 at it; scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci passed whole at 8c4269509 (357 of 357 tests): 'Stats over 3 runs', 'Executed 1 out of 1 test: 1 test passes'.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:74d6b37ad","summary":"Fixed: the test's 150 concurrent seat requests now go at most 64 at a time (IN_FLIGHT), below macOS's kern.ipc.somaxconn of 128","supersedes":"7a6aa55ffe54d8b6f2dbab9c7186bd9d6a1e7d375d798bc7431b1cfb70a60397","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T14:50:49.976807Z","id":"34536e197e06f8eaf7da917ce175668adec2b5c19d0778dedfb6c12c6f529170","body":{"detail":"bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__2 failed twice before 74d6b37ad (Connection reset by peer at api_seats.rs:80) and passed with --runs_per_test=3 at it; scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci passed whole at 8c4269509 (357 of 357 tests): 'Stats over 3 runs', 'Executed 1 out of 1 test: 1 test passes'.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:74d6b37ad","summary":"Fixed: the test's 150 concurrent seat requests now go at most 64 at a time (IN_FLIGHT), below macOS's kern.ipc.somaxconn of 128","supersedes":"77b7b3ccf1aa7500db6928bdc1b9797fc2842e2685a7e5bc0493d998b0f17396","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:18.067706Z","id":"cad76a0926bf6082e87656e446709c48ed0e8206d256c30207c570ede4876b68","body":{"detail":"tests/deferred.rs reruns, on deferred content, the content test modules of the test target it is compiled into, reading that target's clax_split cfg, so it must be a module of crates/clax-server/tests/integration.rs, in every target, not a library. The MCP and public Clax helpers it sat beside in tests/common moved to clax-testkit (mcp.rs, remotes.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":196},"end":{"line":196},"content_hash":"55653b2a3989f67b681b525ef79b5ab056f03ac86a3a755b78d5e92572e4b2c1"},"summary":"Put the deferred-content rerun in clax-testkit with the other test helpers","supersedes":"6ff421d8b6721035a644e3b409d2ff8aee1ff8b7b9c60da7ec3be37d03ac7a54","tags":["tests","layout","revisit:Bazel's split targets pass the modules they hold another way","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_watch.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:25:11.011604Z","id":"4340bc463837d57d74d238d84b30386616e0bce29df9f3a682a5faf30f2d352d","body":{"detail":"until() here is a verbatim copy of crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs:238-253: it sleeps 50 ms between tries and loops forever (for tries in 0u32..), so a condition that never holds hangs the test until the runner's timeout instead of failing with what it waited for. remote_artifact(public) is copied between api_remote_artifacts.rs:21-34 and api_resolve.rs:30-42 and inlined a third time in There::new (api_remote_watch.rs:33-60); enc() is defined in api_remote_artifacts.rs:15, api_resolve.rs:14 and api_remote_watch.rs:571; code(v) in api_remote_requests.rs:13 and api_remotes.rs:13; There (api_remote_watch.rs:23) and Pair (api_linked.rs:18) each build a local daemon with a ManualSleeper-driven Linked connected to a Public. crates/clax-testkit/src/remotes.rs already holds Public, connect and connect_with.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":239},"content_hash":"ea63fae0fecba9aa3e96578d23faf2608aa5a9510f0c14b2f89c17203de5699f"},"suggested_fix":"Move until (bounded: fail with `what` after a fixed number of tries, or wait on an event instead of sleeping), enc, code, a Public::publish(title, page) -> ID and one connected-pair fixture (local TestServer with ManualSleeper/ManualClock, Public, remote ID) into crates/clax-testkit/src/remotes.rs, and use them from api_linked, api_remote_watch, api_remote_artifacts, api_resolve, api_remote_requests and api_remotes.","summary":"The remote test files copy their helpers from each other instead of clax-testkit's remotes module, and the copied until() polls with no bound","tags":["review","review:ri-quality","tests","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:25:49.074267Z","id":"622f078603f61ff1c28e42ee7d1c247241aee132eb9c45d495958b3093376169","body":{"detail":"This file defines `unfollowed`, `login_path`, `set_cookies`, `proof_of`, `owner_cookie_of` (lines 12-71) and `login_in` (1207-1219), used about 23 times, to do what crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs already offers: `login_page_proof` (275), `owner_login_of` (286, which finds the owner cookie among the Set-Cookie headers), `browser_login` (310, a free function making a code with the token and redeeming it, used once, by crates/clax-server/tests/api_events.rs:378), and `TestServer::login` / `TestServer::login_with` (1561, 1590, the same again with the proof remembered for `proof_for`). `retire` (1221-1236) and `token_status` build requests with the cookie and proof by hand where `TestServer::proof_for` exists. `code_of` (73) duplicates `code` in crates/clax-server/tests/api_confirmations.rs:82.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"256517ed09f857770920034de5d1fbbe88643a906da22341cf053b76f1a43048"},"suggested_fix":"Keep one login helper in clax-testkit: `TestServer::login_with(cookies, next)` returning the response and `TestServer::login` the `OwnerLogin`; make `browser_login` a thin call to the same code or drop it for `ts.login(\"\")`. In api_local_trust.rs, delete `login_path`, `set_cookies`, `proof_of`, `owner_cookie_of` and `login_in` in favour of those, and move a shared `error_code(&Value)` into testkit.","summary":"api_local_trust.rs re-implements the browser-login helpers clax-testkit already has, and testkit has three of its own","tags":["review","review:ri-quality","tests","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:25:49.588372Z","id":"e3f09f06304d0e0468d792b9734a0bc87bb8a8ebd361e6bc8015ba0d3bc6d114","body":{"detail":"login_path, unfollowed, set_cookies, owner_cookie_of and proof_of (lines 13-71) and login_in (1207-1218, used throughout the file) make a login code with the token, redeem it at /login with a no-redirect client and scrape the owner cookie and the page's data-proof: what TestServer::login_with + owner_login_of + TestServer::login (crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs:286-307, 1561-1612) already do, except that login_in returns a tuple instead of OwnerLogin and does not register the proof with proof_for. clax-testkit adds a third copy, the free function browser_login (server.rs:310-327), whose only caller is crates/clax-server/tests/api_events.rs:378, where ts.login(\"\") would do. The same scrape is written again in web/e2e/fixtures.ts ownerSession (:86-95), plugins/pi/test/daemon-fixture.ts:87-93, scripts/perf-daemon.py:482-503 and scripts/smoke-comment-loop.sh:122-140, so a change to the login page's data-proof attribute has seven places to update.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":82},"content_hash":"13431f7f33464fcfb4262f4d26b8e6b2053e4b108486099e5584c7de4fafb84b"},"suggested_fix":"Delete clax_testkit::browser_login and use ts.login(\"\") in api_events.rs. Give TestServer::login_with a `next` parameter (or add login_to(next, cookies)) and replace api_local_trust.rs's login_path/login_in/set_cookies/owner_cookie_of/proof_of with TestServer::login, keeping only the helpers that test the login itself (forged, code_of). Have the two Python scripts share one helper (e.g. a scripts/clax_owner_login.py both import).","summary":"api_local_trust.rs re-implements the browser login that clax-testkit already provides, and clax-testkit itself holds two versions of it","tags":["review","review:ri-quality","tests","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:25:49.588417Z","id":"7a086181edac4c04aad0fcb5c4600de9e0f33ee4f8aa1e81071d011622c6e5e4","body":{"detail":"Both files define the same PAGE constant and enc() (api_remote_artifacts.rs:13-17, api_remote_watch.rs:18 and :571-573). Publishing an artifact on the hosted Public via its CLI is remote_artifact() here (:21-33) and inline in There::new (api_remote_watch.rs:34-62). A browser thread there, a multipart POST with HOST, COOKIE clax_session and ORIGIN headers, is browser_thread() here (:36-57) and There::thread_there (api_remote_watch.rs:108-130), nearly line for line. agent_req() (:73-97) is clax_testkit::remotes::local_req (crates/clax-testkit/src/remotes.rs:151-165) with extra headers and an optional body. until() at api_remote_watch.rs:224-240 is a copy of api_linked.rs:238-254 with one comment line removed. These are the steps every remote test needs; api_remote_requests.rs and api_remotes.rs will want them too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"aed8a1624d2c77cea7b3583f3a985d8a9de75eceef9c9189c4655355dd65706c"},"suggested_fix":"Add to clax_testkit::remotes::Public: publish_page(title) -> artifact ID, and browser_thread(raid, cookie, body) -> thread (the multipart request); give local_req an extra-headers parameter or a builder, and move until() into clax-testkit (e.g. clax_testkit::until) for api_linked.rs and api_remote_watch.rs. Then delete the per-file copies, PAGE and enc included.","summary":"api_remote_artifacts.rs and api_remote_watch.rs each write their own Public helpers for the same steps, and api_remote_watch.rs copies until() from api_linked.rs","tags":["review","review:ri-quality","tests","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_confirmations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:25:49.588463Z","id":"03f743ae6f703f554fb82dd9a8118449b8c0bda0b0216ac05e1635d633a9e6e3","body":{"detail":"browser() (lines 45-66) is TestServer::as_browser (crates/clax-testkit/src/passkey.rs:95-113) plus an optional x-clax-confirmation header; token() (:19-43) is the request half of TestServer::confirmed (crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs:1767-1798) and of the confirm loop in clax_testkit::remotes::connect_with (remotes.rs:201-230), each reading the same header and 202 shape. login_now (:88-90) only wraps ts.login(\"\").cookie. code() (:82-84) is the fifteenth copy of `v[\"error\"][\"code\"].as_str()` across crates/clax-server/tests (api_remote_requests.rs:13 is the sixteenth). as_browser is general (cookie plus its proof) but sits in passkey.rs, so tests outside passkeys do not find it.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"32efa9f89d32b8e7b2dcca86b891a61c89cdf4c240bd9f43089373db6c190aa3"},"suggested_fix":"Move as_browser to server.rs and give it (or a sibling) an optional confirmation ID; add a TestServer::token_call(method, path, body, confirm) -> (u16, Value) that checks the held header like token() does, and have confirmed() and connect_with use it. Add clax_testkit::error_code(&Value) and replace the per-file code() copies, starting with the ones this branch added. Delete login_now.","summary":"api_confirmations.rs's request helpers duplicate TestServer::as_browser and TestServer::confirmed with only a confirmation header added","tags":["review","review:ri-quality","tests","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_watch.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:29:47.321916Z","id":"6b814d12d655f1d8291c073eed983fa075ef82b6f972a47b38a58ee631a2c847","body":{"detail":"The copies hold: until() at crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_watch.rs:224-239 matches crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs:238-253; remote_artifact() at api_remote_artifacts.rs:21-34 and api_resolve.rs:30-42, inlined in There::new (api_remote_watch.rs:42-51); enc() at api_remote_artifacts.rs:15, api_resolve.rs:14, api_remote_watch.rs:571; There (api_remote_watch.rs:23) and Pair (api_linked.rs:18) build the same ManualSleeper-driven Linked pair. But the unbounded until() is on main already (main d7812795c, crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs:238), and its doc comment (api_remote_watch.rs:220-222) says it has no wall-clock limit on purpose: AGENTS.md ('Tests are fast and load-tolerant ... no wall-clock budgets in any check') rules out a fixed count of 50 ms sleeps, which is such a budget. code(v) is a repo-wide pattern (about 20 test files, such as api_tags.rs:15 and api_people.rs:20), not one this branch introduced. What remains is moving the remote helpers into crates/clax-testkit/src/remotes.rs (which has Public, connect and connect_with): a tidy-up.","kind":"comment","references":"4340bc463837d57d74d238d84b30386616e0bce29df9f3a682a5faf30f2d352d","summary":"downgraded: comment — the helpers are copied, but the unbounded until() is main's deliberate design and a bounded try count would add a forbidden budget","tags":["verified:downgraded","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:30:17.463457Z","id":"78487bd5a70c240226ffb4db5a09f8d6094b15f5619fe17234c31ae9efcec2a5","body":{"detail":"login_in (crates/clax-server/tests/api_local_trust.rs:1207-1218) is TestServer::login(cookies) (crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs, login/login_with/owner_login_of) returning a tuple, and clax_testkit::browser_login (server.rs:310-327) has one caller, crates/clax-server/tests/api_events.rs:378, where ts.login(\"\") fits. But login_path (api_local_trust.rs:23-34) is called directly in about ten tests (lines 132, 199, 223, 249, 303, 346, 603, 717, 764, 976) that exercise the login with a chosen next, a late or reused code, and its expires_in, so it cannot be replaced by TestServer::login as the fix proposes; set_cookies serves those too. The duplication is test-only, and the copies in Python, shell and TypeScript scripts cannot share one Rust helper. Test-helper tidying, not a risk: suggestion.","kind":"comment","references":"e3f09f06304d0e0468d792b9734a0bc87bb8a8ebd361e6bc8015ba0d3bc6d114","summary":"downgraded: suggestion — login_in duplicates TestServer::login, but most of the named helpers test the login itself and must stay","tags":["verified:downgraded","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:30:17.463797Z","id":"49054e9b103b440ee1527263f954f9a1848844fd9d9d3d55cf02e6935d5e016d","body":{"detail":"Confirmed duplicates: PAGE and enc() in crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_artifacts.rs:13-17 and api_remote_watch.rs:18, :571-573; remote_artifact() (:21-33) vs the publish in There::new (api_remote_watch.rs:42-52); browser_thread() (:36-57) vs There::thread_there (api_remote_watch.rs:106-130) line for line; agent_req() (:73-97) is clax_testkit::remotes::local_req (crates/clax-testkit/src/remotes.rs:151-165) plus headers and an optional body; until() at api_remote_watch.rs:224-240 equals api_linked.rs:238-254. No behaviour at risk, test code only, so suggestion (as the sibling finding 03f743ae on api_confirmations.rs is).","kind":"comment","references":"7a086181edac4c04aad0fcb5c4600de9e0f33ee4f8aa1e81071d011622c6e5e4","summary":"downgraded: suggestion — the remote test helpers and until() are duplicated, a test-only tidy","tags":["verified:downgraded","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_confirmations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:30:17.464132Z","id":"0bb3ef73a854665d1b567ca80382a9a7f49c1c2ed7e0f20f2becaeb8b8962881","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_confirmations.rs:45-66 browser() equals TestServer::as_browser (crates/clax-testkit/src/passkey.rs:95-113) plus an optional confirmation header; token() :19-43 is the request half of TestServer::confirmed (crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs, about 1767-1798) with the same header read; login_now :88-90 is ts.login(\"\").cookie. grep -ln 'fn code(v: &Value)' crates/clax-server/tests/*.rs counts 18 files, more than the finding's fifteen.","kind":"comment","references":"03f743ae6f703f554fb82dd9a8118449b8c0bda0b0216ac05e1635d633a9e6e3","summary":"confirmed: browser()/token()/login_now/code() duplicate testkit helpers","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:30:32.125057Z","id":"a4eca806d236045c3c4a2422fe3cdb5e17cd199af94c18eb823f483129e4f4a9","body":{"detail":"login_path (crates/clax-server/tests/api_local_trust.rs:23-34) returns the unredeemed path with a chosen `next` and asserts expires_in 120; the tests at lines 132, 199, 223, 249, 303, 603, 717, 764 and 976 redeem it twice, late, with forged headers or a custom next, and expect non-200 answers. TestServer::login_with (crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs:1590-1615) hard-codes next \"/\" and asserts 200, and testkit has no path-only helper. set_cookies backs the `is_empty()` assertions at lines 111, 123, 197, 207, 239, 378, 489, 597 and 760, which no testkit helper offers. What does duplicate: login_in (1207-1219) is TestServer::login (server.rs:1561) without the proof bookkeeping, and owner_cookie_of (64-71) is the search in owner_login_of (server.rs:286-300); proof_of already wraps testkit's login_page_proof.","kind":"comment","references":"622f078603f61ff1c28e42ee7d1c247241aee132eb9c45d495958b3093376169","summary":"downgraded: comment — only login_in (and owner_cookie_of) duplicate testkit; login_path and set_cookies cannot be replaced by it","tags":["verified:downgraded","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_watch.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:31:56.111891Z","id":"5498196bad0533f552ccb8176a4e3d32e7eef8f34ca3409a5f6ceed992df6adf","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Its holding part (the remote test helpers copied between files) is 7a086181's; verification reply 6b814d12 shows the unbounded until() is deliberate.","supersedes":"4340bc463837d57d74d238d84b30386616e0bce29df9f3a682a5faf30f2d352d","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:31:56.210472Z","id":"60d785f8127fed50a5218d19756b023b1d911dd0fd1cbf20a00e0cc117827c03","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Verification reply a4eca806 narrows it to login_in and owner_cookie_of, which e3f09f06 already covers.","supersedes":"622f078603f61ff1c28e42ee7d1c247241aee132eb9c45d495958b3093376169","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_confirmations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T06:40:52.842142Z","id":"9b5ab9771880b132c8074ad16c7bf7eb9046b6376c8422d9f678a84a6be8cf1c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:adc2294c9","summary":"as_browser moved to crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs beside as_browser_confirming and token_call (which checks the held confirmation header; confirmed() shares its request), and clax_testkit::error_code replaces the code() copy in api_confirmations.rs, whose token/browser/code/login_now helpers are deleted. Not done here: clax_testkit::remotes::connect_with's confirm loop and the code() copies in other test files (api_remote_requests.rs among them), left to the files' own work. //crates/clax-server:all passes.","supersedes":"03f743ae6f703f554fb82dd9a8118449b8c0bda0b0216ac05e1635d633a9e6e3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T06:41:39.842883Z","id":"5339cf0e9fb153f8cefa54cdd6028cb5b4c6e9adf06fd4c65aae6353ac2690c9","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_local_trust.rs logs a browser in with TestServer::login (login_in's callers) and clax_testkit::owner_login_of (the renewed, second and new-code logins); the LAN-address login reads its proof with login_page_proof. api_events.rs uses ts.login, and clax_testkit::browser_login, its one caller gone, is deleted. login_path, set_cookies and unfollowed stay: they test the login itself (a chosen next, a late or reused code, expires_in, the cookies' attributes). The Python, shell and TypeScript copies were not touched.","kind":"comment","references":"e3f09f06304d0e0468d792b9734a0bc87bb8a8ebd361e6bc8015ba0d3bc6d114","summary":"Done in part (git:adc2294c9): login_in, owner_cookie_of and proof_of are gone from api_local_trust.rs, and clax_testkit::browser_login with them","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_remote_artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T06:34:51.604103Z","id":"8cca31040b486a9e3bf25a79c3c52cd18776974196d1eaa3bc14cce01289e045","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6ef3bc010c8ce1de56ca5e7bb25631217bcaaaca","summary":"Fixed: clax_testkit::until (still unbounded: no wall-clock budget) replaces the copies in api_linked and api_remote_watch; clax_testkit::remotes gains PAGE, enc, Public::publish, Public::browser_thread and Public::revoke, used by api_remote_artifacts, api_remote_watch, api_resolve, api_remotes and api_linked instead of their copies. agent_req stays in api_remote_artifacts (extra headers and an optional body). Tests: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all, 7 targets PASSED.","supersedes":"7a086181edac4c04aad0fcb5c4600de9e0f33ee4f8aa1e81071d011622c6e5e4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/api_visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T07:09:40.009009Z","id":"650e2989f23a98ebfdba92d98bba88e675a6b4ddb327569f9885f5d79516427f","body":{"detail":"Observed in review of the remote-instances fix branches: the assertion all.matches(OWNER_ASKS).count() == 1 (line 2452) failed with 0 in about one run of fifteen, in code those branches did not change. A likely cause is ordering: clients.follow() takes the owner's comment before the hooks read their tiers, so the hooks find it delivered already in some runs. Not investigated further.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2427},"end":{"line":2465},"content_hash":"1bc407f37480a645d02ca2f6f52321da43b423c23a9aeae1c46e05022d8cce1d"},"summary":"hook_tiers_are_filtered_for_owner_agents fails about 1 run in 15: the hooks see 0 owner asks after clients.follow()","tags":["flaky","tests","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
